00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:27,260
But I know that true friends may be hard
to leave, but they're impossible to forget.

243
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:31,217
And even though his stay wasn't
as long as we would have liked,

244
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:33,560
we're lucky we knew him at all.

245
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:35,200
Thank you, Joy.

246
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:37,800
Goodbye, Atem.

247
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:39,140
And good luck.

248
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:40,940
Hey, Pharaoh!

249
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:44,917
I hate to break the terrible news to
you, but you're not going anywhere.

250
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,882
Because everything you've given
us stays right here in our hearts.

251
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:50,090
Right.

252
00:17:50,173 --> 00:17:53,020
Like we always say, it's your move!

253
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:26,840
He's gone.

254
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:30,660
Well, Pharaoh, goodbye.

255
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:38,540
What's that? An earthquake.

256
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:42,200
It's the Millennium Stone!

257
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,040
The items are gone!

258
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:47,917
And we should do the same.

259
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,640
Run for your lives! He's right! Let's go!

260
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,360
Now that the Pharaoh has
returned to the next world,

261
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:21,077
the Millennium Items have been
permanently sealed And our

262
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:24,395
duty as the Pharaoh's Tomb
Keepers is finally complete.

263
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:26,060
So this is the end?

264
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:27,960
Feels weird. Yeah.

265
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:30,085
What were you geeks expecting?

266
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:33,000
Fireworks, sappy music, something.

267
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:36,017
At least make one of your
little wrap-up speeches, Yug.

268
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:40,600
Well, sometimes the end of one adventure
is just the beginning of another.

269
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:42,200
Ah, much better.
